\begin{IDEA}
**Title**: Quantifying Idiosyncratic Noise Impact on Factor Mimicking Portfolio (FMP) Efficiency

**Description**: This research evaluates the efficacy of reconstructing the four latent factors (MKT, SMB, HML, WML) using a constrained optimization approach that maps observed stock returns and market capitalizations to the underlying factor space. By applying a rolling-window FMP construction, we quantify the tracking error introduced by the 3.5% idiosyncratic monthly volatility against the theoretical factor returns provided in `factors.csv`. We will specifically test whether weighting schemes based on inverse-variance or market-cap-neutralization can mitigate the impact of this noise on portfolio Sharpe ratios compared to the ground-truth loadings. The final objective is to define the threshold of idiosyncratic noise at which FMP reconstruction fails to span the cross-section, providing a benchmark for the robustness of factor-based asset pricing in low-signal environments.
\end{IDEA}


